   "conclusion": {
    "diagnosis": "Intermittent inspection failures on batch 2: jobs 14 (tick 1354), 19 (1702), and 20 (1768) failed inspection while jobs 15-18 passed between them (E2, E3), so the fault is condition-dependent/intermittent rather than progressive degradation (H4 is weakened by the passes between failures). All three failing jobs finished on CNC-07 immediately before inspection - job 14 finished CNC-07 at 1353 then failed at 1354; job 19 finished CNC-07 at 1701 then failed at 1702; job 20 finished CNC-07 at 1767 then failed at 1768 (E6, E8) - but it is unverified whether passing jobs 17 and 18 also used CNC-07 (Q13 open) or which material lot the failing jobs ran (Q14, Q17 open). Material batch 3 opened at tick 1310 (E6) before job 14's failure, yet jobs 15-18 passed afterward, so batch 3 alone does not explain the failures (H5 unproven); the loading-door opening at 1729-1740 (E8) postdates job 19's failure, so it cannot explain all failures. Root cause is not isolated: CNC-07, material lot, or another condition remain possible.",
